# --param msil_roundtrip=1 (the round-trip leg, Design.md 5.5; plan 5.12.3
# lists it among the %if legs of %{msil_prog}) makes %{msil_prog} disassemble
# each level's program image <t>.<L>.d/prog.exe, reassemble the listing with
# the .NET ildasm and ilasm that msil/utils/tools/msil-tools.proj pins into an
# EXE, <t>.<L>.rt.exe (not the .rt.dll of %{msil_c} under asm, which
# ../legs/roundtrip-composites.test covers), require the two listings to match
# (msil-verify.py --roundtrip) and run <t>.<L>.rt.exe against the test's own
# .expected file into <t>.<L>.rt.out. %{msil_c} under msil_pipeline=lto is
# %{msil_prog} of its one source and does the same. The leg passes whenever
# its tests pass, so a lit.cfg.py that dropped the round trip from
# prog_pipeline, wrote the image back as a DLL or ran something else than
# the reassembled image would leave it green without round-tripping the
# program. A nested lit with -a prints every command it ran, so for each
# level that msil_opt_levels selects (features msil-opt-<L> of
# lit.local.cfg) the output must show both commands:
# (1) for Inputs/nested/roundtrip/rt-prog.test, %{msil_prog} of two sources
#     under the default pipeline (asm), and
# (2) for Inputs/nested/roundtrip/rt-c.c, %{msil_c} under
#     msil_pipeline=lto (which needs msil-ld and llvm-ar configured, as
#     lit-config.test's (7) shows);
# and the tests must pass. (3) The control: without msil_roundtrip=1 the same
# %{msil_prog} runs no round trip. The stand-ins of lit.local.cfg build the
# programs (no clang or msil-ld runs), and the nested runs use the local
# runner, as in pipelines.test. msil_roundtrip=1 is a configuration error
# without the pinned tools, so the test needs them (feature
# msil-roundtrip-tools of lit.local.cfg; the gates and CI restore them).
# REQUIRES: msil-roundtrip-tools

# (1)
# RUN: %{harness_lit} -a --param msil_runner=local --param msil_linux_sysroot= --param msil_roundtrip=1 %S/Inputs/nested/roundtrip/rt-prog.test > %t.prog.log 2>&1
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.prog.log "^PASS: MSIL :: harness/prog/Inputs/nested/roundtrip/rt-prog\.test "
# RUN: %if msil-opt-O0 %{ %{harness_check} contains %t.prog.log "^# executed command: .*msil-verify\.py'? --roundtrip --ildasm .* --ilasm .* '?--output=.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O0\.rt\.exe'? '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O0\.d/prog\.exe'?$" "^# executed command: .*msil-run\.py'? --expect-os .* --expect '?.*\Wroundtrip\Wrt-prog'? --out '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O0\.rt\.out'? '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O0\.rt\.exe'?$" %}
# RUN: %if msil-opt-O1 %{ %{harness_check} contains %t.prog.log "^# executed command: .*msil-verify\.py'? --roundtrip --ildasm .* --ilasm .* '?--output=.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O1\.rt\.exe'? '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O1\.d/prog\.exe'?$" "^# executed command: .*msil-run\.py'? --expect-os .* --expect '?.*\Wroundtrip\Wrt-prog'? --out '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O1\.rt\.out'? '?.*rt-prog\.test\.tmp\.O1\.rt\.exe'?$" %}
